To solve this problem, we can use the fact that any power of three is divisible by 3. Therefore, we can keep dividing the given number by 3 until we get 1 or a number that is not divisible by 3. If we get 1, then the number is a power of three, otherwise it is not.

Here is the Java code to implement this solution:

```
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }
    while (n % 3 == 0) {
        n /= 3;
    }
    return n == 1;
}
```

This solution has a time complexity of O(log n) and a space complexity of O(1), which is efficient and does not require loops or recursion.
